    "whatIsMoralStand": {
        "visited": false,
        "dialogue": [
            {
                "charID": "o-brian",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "o'brian",
                "text": "Moral standing is..."
            },
            {
                "charID": "o-brian",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "o'brian",
                "text": "Well, why don't we just ask the supercomputer?"
            },
            {
                "charID": "o-brian",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "o'brian",
                "text": "Aida, what is &ldquo;moral standing&rdquo;?"
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Several fundamental qualities or characteristics are potentially qualifying an artificial intelligence system for moral standing."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "These ideas draw on philosophical concepts about what makes an entity worthy of moral consideration, often by analogy to humans, animals, or other entities we currently grant some form of moral status or rights."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Some of the key qualities and characteristics are cognitive capabilities, psychological capacities, philosophical concepts, and behavioral and relational considerations."
            },
            {
                "charID": "o-brian",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "o'brian",
                "text": "Where do you want to start, your honor?"
            }
        ],
        "choice": [
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "Let's discuss cognitive capabilities.",
                "nextScene": "discussCC"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "Let's discuss psychological capacities.",
                "nextScene": "discussPsyCap"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "Let's discuss philosophical concepts.",
                "nextScene": "discussPhilCon"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "Let's discuss behavioral and relational considerations.",
                "nextScene": "discussBRC"
            }
        ]
    },
    "discussCC": {
        "visited": false,
        "dialogue": [
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Some important cognitive capabilities of beings with moral standing are intelligence, rationality, autonomy, and agency. Which would you like to discuss?"
            }
        ],
        "choice": [
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is intelligence?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsInt"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is rationality?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsRat"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is autonomy?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsAuto"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is agency?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsAg"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "Actually, let's talk about something else.",
                "nextScene": "whatIsMoralStand"
            }
        ]
    },
    "whatIsInt": {
        "visited": false,
        "dialogue": [
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Intelligence is often discussed, particularly regarding reaching human-like or superintelligence levels."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Human-level intelligence might be considered a sufficient condition by some."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "However, intelligence itself is hard to define and measure for AIs, and the moral relevance might stem more from associated capacities like sentience rather than intelligence per se."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Would you like to discuss another cognitive capability?"
            }
        ],
        "choice": [
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is rationality?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsRat"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is autonomy?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsAuto"
            },
            {
                "type": "spoken",
                "text": "What is agency?",
                "nextScene": "whatIsAg"
            }
        ]
    },
    "whatIsRat": {
        "visited": false,
        "dialogue": [
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "High degrees of rationality are sometimes emphasized, particularly in Kantian or social contract approaches to morality, as necessary for reflecting on and justifying moral principles."
            },
            {
                "charID": "aida",
                "type": "spoken",
                "charName": "aida",
                "text": "Would you like to discuss another cognitive capability?"
            }
        ],
        "choice": [
